{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the DX-A1 authoring skill at head d88ac126ede1a8eff9f2122324ac4ab122745872, tree 8cbd5572c02f9018d93763eba9a02e59fd4a6797, for request c9d4e517 and review request cdc8f69a. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds six commits to main b98968e5 and changes 24 paths:\n- the seven-file `skills/dap-application` tree;\n- four plugin manifests and catalogs;\n- the platform skill mapping in the release scripts and plan, with its owning test;\n- the canonical-link mapping in `check-doc-links` and its fixture, now listed in `scripts/test.mjs`;\n- a starter case in the CLI's application-example test;\n- the creation-versions fixture repair;\n- the release guide, and the implementation note and its manifest.\n\nI read the implementation note first, then the diff, the skill, the manifests, the failed gate and the follow-up evidence.\n\n## Against request c9d4e517\n\n1. The skill. Resolved.\n   - `SKILL.md` gives the write, check and fix loop and links the starter and the authoring reference. The starter is a complete five-file package: definition, signal, manifest with a declared view, scenario and entry.\n   - The new CLI case runs the real `dap check` on the starter. It reports 2 definitions validated, 11 scenario steps with replay through 4, and 2 projection checks.\n   - The skill names only the checkout's CLI for `check`, `pack` and `install`. It adds no hook, connector or remote service.\n2. Independent first runs. Resolved, with honest limits.\n   - V1 and V2 failed and stay failed, and their calibration copies are labeled as calibration.\n   - V3, a new agent with the third skill version, passed its single permitted check at C: 20 steps, replay through 7, and 3 projections.\n   - The skill's Git tree at the head is 5c77a46a, the same tree as at C, so the passing run covers the skill bytes that ship.\n3. The carrier. Resolved.\n   - Under ruling 97c503ba, `@generalbusiness/dap-platform` carries the skill as `skills` files, and the CLI stays private.\n   - The producer copies committed blob bytes and modes, within bounds on depth, entries, files and size. It refuses missing, changed, untracked, nonregular and symlinked assets. The checker recomputes the inventory and compares the source, the stage and the actual archive.\n   - The three scratch controls each fail the unchanged named case with an ordinary assertion.\n   - I read the platform archive `0.1.0-dev.4` in the sealed evidence. It has 209 members, including 7 under `skills/dap-application`, all with mode 0644 and byte-identical to the head. Its `files` field lists `dist`, `skills`, `README.md`, `LICENSE` and `NOTICE`, and it has no install scripts.\n4. Plugin manifests. Resolved. Two formats select the same root skill tree. The catalog offers installation, and its `ON_USE` authentication has no authenticated component behind it. The note does not claim host installation or enablement.\n\n## The failed gate and the single-file follow-up\n\nThe ordinary gate at F, 2d40001a with tree d505dfcc, failed one native case: `creation-versions.test.ts:156`, where `native.submit(found)` returned `refused`. The gate stays failed, and the note says so.\n\nThe repair at G, 5bb0f733 with tree 47f074a0, meets the conditions in \"Follow-up after a gate\" in `docs/testing.md`:\n- F to G changes only `packages/scope/test/creation-versions.test.ts`. No other file imports it. Production code, configuration, dependencies and shared helpers are unchanged.\n- The repair replaces `new Date(...).toISOString()` with `timeOf(...)` for the two existing 60-second deadlines. It keeps every original case, assertion, pin, native clock and deadline. The added case is wider, not narrower: it checks the real signed shape and the 60-second arithmetic, and it refuses the noncanonical form.\n- The compiler context whose inputs changed passes, and the whole owning file passes 6 of 6. The gate reached every stage, so no step remained unreached.\n- The control restores the old formatter in the new case, which then fails with an ordinary `AssertionError` on `isSignedIntentShape`. The helper restores the file.\n\nThe repair also fits the evidence. `toISOString()` keeps `.000Z` on an exact-second deadline. The strict time parser refuses that form, and that happens about once in a thousand runs, which agrees with the unchanged file passing 5 of 5 on rerun. The note still calls the cause unproved, which is right. No other signed `notAfter` in the tree uses the old form.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main b98968e5 gives the head tree 8cbd5572.\n- G to the head changes only the note and the manifest, which the documents-only rule covers.\n- I reran the owning files once each, with no whole suite:\n  - `public-release-modules.test.mjs` and `check-doc-links.test.mjs`: 6 of 6;\n  - `creation-versions.test.ts`: 6 of 6;\n  - `application-examples.test.ts`: 3 of 3.\n- The manifest has SHA-256 20c701ff and 41,644 bytes. It follows ruling 4e199bd8:\n  - all 241 listed files match by size and SHA-256;\n  - `finalization` and `operator-inputs` match their digests, and each SHA256SUMS reruns clean, with no unlisted file;\n  - the root SHA256SUMS covers all 2,591 other files, with none unlisted and none writable, and its digest is 5fa88563.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 760 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from b98968e5: one warning, for the manifest over the soft limit, as disclosed.\n- check-commit-messages from b98968e5: 6 checked, 0 flagged.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The plugin descriptions say \"with Claude Code\" and \"with Codex\". The manifest directory names are fixed by each format, but the descriptions can drop the product names under the naming rule. \"Write and check declared dap applications\" serves both.\n2. `check-doc-links` maps only the `github.com/generalbusiness-ai/artroom/blob/main/` prefix. That matches the current origin, but the package manifests already use `generalbusiness-ai/dap`. If the repository moves, the checker will stop checking the skill's links without failing.\n3. Adding `check-doc-links.test.mjs` to `scripts/test.mjs` puts the doc-links fixture in the gate. The release-module witness that the 29 October report names is still not in the list.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe skill is a document tree with a checked starter, and the only code it adds is release mapping. The platform package carries it as files, with no new export, dependency or runtime path. The kernel, the Workers and admission are unchanged. The eight-package plan keeps its guards. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\n- The release copies only committed blobs, and it refuses symlinks, untracked files and mode drift, within size and count bounds.\n- The archive has no install scripts.\n- The plugin catalogs add no hook, connector or authenticated service.\n- The skill tells an agent to run only the checkout's CLI, and it tells them to keep an uncertain original request instead of replacing it.\n\nApproved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nOne canonical skill tree serves the repository plugins and the platform archive, with no copies in the checkout. The release mapping reuses the existing tar boundary and guards. The test repair is four changed lines and one added case. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The single-file follow-up: the repair at G meets the conditions of `docs/testing.md`, and the gate at F stays failed.\n- The request's checks: items 1 to 4 hold in the skill, the starter check, the first-run evidence, the archive and the sealed collection under ruling 4e199bd8.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:54a059dc480cdc103395d254e2860b68ea39f53b","binding":"assigned","head":"d88ac126ede1a8eff9f2122324ac4ab122745872","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f5e09dabad6dda50e101a2867cc9a551587d5449\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:251e087709a844a98dbcc3cce8f2eeec8d032612\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f5e09dabad6dda50e101a2867cc9a551587d5449","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}